{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-84070f8c4e6ed34c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "900\t[\n901\t0\n902\t,\n903\t100\n904\t)\n905\t⊔\n906\t𝒮\n907\t,\n908\t\\displaystyle\\sqcup\\ \\texttt{DUR}_{[1,201)}\\sqcup\\texttt{VEL}_{[0,32)}\\sqcup\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{[0,100)}\\sqcup\\mathcal{S},\n909\t(1)\n910\tso\n911\t|\n912\t𝒱\n913\tmusic\n914\t|\n915\t=\n916\t16\n917\t+\n918\t129\n919\t+\n920\t128\n921\t+\n922\t200\n923\t+\n924\t32\n925\t+\n926\t100\n927\t+\n928\t4\n929\t=\n930\t609\n931\t|\\mathcal{V}_{\\text{music}}|=16{+}129{+}128{+}200{+}32{+}100{+}4=609\n932\t. Formally, a piece\n933\ty\n934\t=\n935\t{\n936\t(\n937\tp\n938\tj\n939\t,\n940\to\n941\tj\n942\t,\n943\td\n944\tj\n945\t,\n946\tv\n947\tj\n948\t,\n949\tc\n950\tj\n951\t)\n952\t}\n953\tj\n954\t=\n955\t1\n956\tN\n957\ty=\\{(p_{j},o_{j},d_{j},v_{j},c_{j})\\}_{j=1}^{N}\n958\t(pitch, onset, duration, velocity, channel) is serialized in onset order as\n959\tR\n960\tPMT\n961\t(\n962\ty\n963\t)\n964\t=\n965\t[\n966\t\\displaystyle R_{\\text{PMT}}(y)=\\big[\n967\tTSHIFT\n968\tq\n969\tt\n970\t​\n971\t(\n972\tΔ\n973\tj\n974\t)\n975\t,\n976\t(\n977\tTRACK\n978\tc\n979\tj\n980\t​\n981\tPROG\n982\tg\n983\tj\n984\t)\n985\t,\n986\t\\displaystyle\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{q_{t}(\\Delta_{j})},(\\texttt{TRACK}_{c_{j}}\\,\\texttt{PROG}_{g_{j}}),\n987\tPITCH\n988\tp\n989\tj\n990\t,\n991\tDUR\n992\tq\n993\td\n994\t​\n995\t(\n996\td\n997\tj\n998\t)\n999\t,\n1000\tVEL\n1001\tq\n1002\tv\n1003\t​\n1004\t(\n1005\tv\n1006\tj\n1007\t)\n1008\t]\n1009\tj\n1010\t=\n1011\t1\n1012\tN\n1013\t,\n1014\t\\displaystyle\\texttt{PITCH}_{p_{j}},\\texttt{DUR}_{q_{d}(d_{j})},\\texttt{VEL}_{q_{v}(v_{j})}\\big]_{j=1}^{N},\n1015\t(2)\n1016\twhich is\n1017\tschematic\n1018\t: the leading\n1019\tTSHIFT\n1020\tcarries the gap to the previous onset and is omitted when\n1021\tΔ\n1022\tj\n1023\t=\n1024\t0\n1025\t\\Delta_{j}{=}0\n1026\t, and\n1027\t(\n1028\tTRACK\n1029\t,\n1030\tPROG\n1031\t)\n1032\t(\\texttt{TRACK},\\texttt{PROG})\n1033\tare emitted only when the instrument changes (the exact run-length gating is in Appendix\n1034\tB\n1035\t). With base time unit\n1036\tτ\n1037\t=\n1038\t10\n1039\t\\tau{=}10\n1040\tms and backward inter-onset gap\n1041\tΔ\n1042\tj\n1043\t=\n1044\to\n1045\tj\n1046\t−\n1047\to\n1048\tj\n1049\t−\n1050\t1\n1051\t\\Delta_{j}\\!=\\!o_{j}\\!-\\!o_{j-1}\n1052\t(taking\n1053\to\n1054\t0\n1055\t=\n1056\t0\n1057\to_{0}{=}0\n1058\t), the three quantizers are deterministic and fixed,\n1059\tq\n1060\tt\n1061\t​\n1062\t(\n1063\tΔ\n1064\t)\n1065\t\\displaystyle q_{t}(\\Delta)\n1066\t=\n1067\tmin\n1068\t(\n1069\t⌊\n1070\tΔ\n1071\t/\n1072\tτ\n1073\t⌉\n1074\t,\n1075\t99\n1076\t)\n1077\t,\n1078\t\\displaystyle=\\min\\!\\big(\\lfloor\\Delta/\\tau\\rceil,\\,99\\big),\n1079\tq\n1080\td\n1081\t​\n1082\t(\n1083\td\n1084\t)\n1085\t\\displaystyle q_{d}(d)\n1086\t=\n1087\tclip\n1088\t(\n1089\t⌊\n1090\td\n1091\t/\n1092\tτ\n1093\t⌉\n1094\t,\n1095\t1\n1096\t,\n1097\t200\n1098\t)\n1099\t,\n1100\t\\displaystyle=\\mathrm{clip}\\!\\big(\\lfloor d/\\tau\\rceil,\\,1,\\,200\\big),\n1101\tq\n1102\tv\n1103\t​\n1104\t(\n1105\tv\n1106\t)\n1107\t\\displaystyle q_{v}(v)\n1108\t=\n1109\t⌊\n1110\t32\n1111\t​\n1112\tv\n1113\t/\n1114\t128\n1115\t⌋\n1116\t,\n1117\t\\displaystyle=\\lfloor 32v/128\\rfloor,\n1118\t(3)\n1119\tso time-shift and duration share one 10 ms lattice and velocity is binned to 32 levels; simultaneous onsets give\n1120\tΔ\n1121\tj\n1122\t=\n1123\t0\n1124\t⇒\n1125\tTSHIFT\n1126\t0\n1127\t\\Delta_{j}{=}0\\Rightarrow\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{0}\n1128\t, so chords are runs of pitches at zero shift, longer gaps are tiled by repeated maximal shift tokens, and\n1129\tTRACK\n1130\t/\n1131\tPROG\n1132\tare emitted only on instrument change, giving\n1133\t≈\n1134\t4\n1135\t\\approx\\!4\n1136\ttokens/note (full procedure and a worked C-major-triad example in Appendix\n1137\tB\n1138\t). Two design choices define the representation.\n1139\tPerformance resolution\n1140\t: 10 ms time-shifts and 32-level velocities preserve the micro-timing and dynamics that beat grids quantize away, with clean model-free evidence in the round-trip\n1141\tonset error\n1142\t(\n1143\t2.3\n1144\t2.3\n1145\tms median on real music versus\n1146\t53\n1147\t53\n1148\tms for beat grids). The mechanism is precise: beat-grid tokenizers (REMI, TSD) place each onset on a tempo-relative grid of\n1149\tR\n1150\tR\n1151\tsteps per beat, encoding it as a bar index plus an in-bar position,\n1152\tpos\n1153\t(\n1154\to\n1155\t)\n1156\t=\n1157\t⌊\n1158\t(\n1159\to\n1160\t−\n1161\tbar\n1162\t(\n1163\to\n1164\t)\n1165\t)\n1166\t/\n1167\tρ\n1168\t⌉\n1169\t,\n1170\tρ\n1171\t=\n1172\t60\n1173\tB\n1174\t⋅\n1175\tR\n1176\ts\n1177\t,\n1178\t\\mathrm{pos}(o)=\\big\\lfloor(o-\\mathrm{bar}(o))/\\rho\\big\\rceil,\\qquad\\rho=\\tfrac{60}{B\\cdot R}\\ \\text{s},\n1179\t(4)\n1180\twhose step\n1181\tρ\n1182\t\\rho\n1183\tis\n1184\ttempo-dependent\n1185\t(\n1186\tB\n1187\tB\n1188\tis beats-per-minute) and bounded by the grid density\n1189\tR\n1190\tR\n1191\t(typically\n1192\tR\n1193\t∈\n1194\t{\n1195\t4\n1196\t,\n1197\t8\n1198\t}\n1199\tR\\!\\in\\!\\{4,8\\}\n1200\t, i.e.\n1201\tρ\n1202\t≈\n1203\t63\n1204\t\\rho\\!\\approx\\!63\n1205\tto\n1206\t125\n1207\t125\n1208\tms at\n1209\t120\n1210\t120\n1211\tBPM, coarser when slower). PMT instead encodes the raw inter-onset interval\n1212\tΔ\n1213\tj\n1214\t\\Delta_{j}\n1215\ton the fixed\n1216\tτ\n1217\t=\n1218\t10\n1219\t\\tau{=}10\n1220\tms lattice of Eq. (\n1221\t3\n1222\t), independent of tempo and metre, so swing and rubato survive rather than snapping to a grid line. That single substitution, continuous performance time for quantized score time, is the one variable the controlled swap of Component 3 isolates. We also report a chord-time ceiling (\n1223\t39.1\n1224\t%\n1225\t39.1\\%\n1226\tvs. REMI/Beat-TSD\n1227\t35.5\n1228\t%\n1229\t35.5\\%\n1230\t, ABC\n1231\t32.5\n1232\t%\n1233\t32.5\\%\n1234\t) but read it with care: because the 10 ms lattice snaps near-simultaneous onsets to\n1235\tTSHIFT\n1236\t0\n1237\t, PMT’s ceiling sits within a couple of points of the raw reference and its sign is subset-dependent, which is why we treat onset error, not the chord-time ceiling, as the primary expressiveness signal (Appendix\n1238\tB\n1239\t).\n1240\tFlat single stream\n1241\t: unlike grouped encodings that need multi-head outputs, PMT’s stream is consumed by any single-softmax LLM, and it interleaves all instruments so the model attends across the full arrangement. Decoding is deterministic and total, so validity is\n1242\t0.99\n1243\t0.99\n1244\t–\n1245\t1.00\n1246\t1.00\n1247\t, and because every token names one parameter the representation is disentangled by construction.\n1248\tThe decoder is exact on the quantization lattice: encode\n1249\t→\n1250\t\\rightarrow\n1251\tdecode is the identity on quantized pitch, onset, duration, velocity and channel, so every deviation from a source piece is attributable to quantization, never to the serialization. Proposition\n1252\t1\n1253\tin Appendix\n1254\tB\n1255\tstates and proves this, with the error bounds (\n1256\t±\n1257\t\\pm\n1258\t5 ms onset,\n1259\t±\n1260\t\\pm\n1261\t5 ms duration,\n1262\t±\n1263\t\\pm\n1264\t2 velocity levels).\n1265\tComponent 2: LLM Integration Recipe\n1266\tThe recipe converts a pretrained text LLM into a text-to-music generator with minimal surgery. (i)\n1267\tVocabulary extension\n1268\t: the 609 music symbols are appended to the backbone tokenizer (Qwen3.5\n1269\t(Yang\n1270\tet al.\n1271\t2025\n1272\t)\n1273\t, 248k text tokens) as mean-initialized embeddings, no architecture change, one softmax. (ii)\n1274\tCaption-masked SFT\n1275\t: each example concatenates caption tokens\n1276\tc\n1277\t=\n1278\t(\n1279\tc\n1280\t1\n1281\t,\n1282\t…\n1283\t,\n1284\tc\n1285\tm\n1286\t)\n1287\tc{=}(c_{1},\\dots,c_{m})\n1288\tand the music stream\n1289\tx\n1290\t=\n1291\tR\n1292\tPMT\n1293\t​\n1294\t(\n1295\ty\n1296\t)\n1297\t=\n1298\t(\n1299\tx\n1300\t1\n1301\t,\n1302\t…\n1303\t,\n1304\tx\n1305\tT\n1306\t)\n1307\tx{=}R_{\\text{PMT}}(y){=}(x_{1},\\dots,x_{T})\n1308\tinto one\n1309\t1024\n1310\t1024\n1311\t-token block\n1312\ts\n1313\ts\n1314\t. With a per-position mask\n1315\tℓ\n1316\ti\n1317\t=\n1318\t𝟙\n1319\t​\n1320\t[\n1321\ti\n1322\t>\n1323\tm\n1324\t]\n1325\t\\ell_{i}{=}\\mathbb{1}[i{>}m]\n1326\t, the backbone minimizes the\n1327\tcaption-masked\n1328\tautoregressive negative log-likelihood over caption–score pairs\n1329\t𝒟\n1330\t\\mathcal{D}\n1331\t,\n1332\tℒ\n1333\t​\n1334\t(\n1335\tθ\n1336\t)\n1337\t=\n1338\t−\n1339\t𝔼\n1340\t(\n1341\tc\n1342\t,\n1343\ty\n1344\t)\n1345\t∼\n1346\t𝒟\n1347\t​\n1348\t1\n1349\t|\n1350\t{\n1351\ti\n1352\t:\n1353\tℓ\n1354\ti\n1355\t=\n1356\t1\n1357\t}\n1358\t|\n1359\t​\n1360\t∑\n1361\ti\n1362\t=\n1363\t1\n1364\tm\n1365\t+\n1366\tT\n1367\tℓ\n1368\ti\n1369\t​\n1370\tlog\n1371\t⁡\n1372\tp\n1373\tθ\n1374\t​\n1375\t(\n1376\ts\n1377\ti\n1378\t∣\n1379\ts\n1380\t<\n1381\ti\n1382\t)\n1383\t,\n1384\t\\mathcal{L}(\\theta)=-\\,\\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\\sim\\mathcal{D}}\\;\\frac{1}{|\\{i:\\ell_{i}{=}1\\}|}\\sum_{i=1}^{m+T}\\ell_{i}\\,\\log p_{\\theta}\\big(s_{i}\\mid s_{<i}\\big),\n1385\t(5)\n1386\tso gradients flow only from the\n1387\tT\n1388\tT\n1389\tmusic positions. Causal attention over the shared block means the music tokens still attend the full caption, so conditioning is preserved though the caption is not a prediction target. (iii)\n1390\tMusic-constrained decoding\n1391\t: at inference, logits are renormalized over the music range only,\n1392\tp\n1393\t~\n1394\tθ\n1395\t​\n1396\t(\n1397\tv\n1398\t∣\n1399\tc\n1400\t,\n1401\tx\n1402\t<\n1403\tt\n1404\t)\n1405\t∝\n1406\tp\n1407\tθ\n1408\t​\n1409\t(\n1410\tv\n1411\t∣\n1412\tc\n1413\t,\n1414\tx\n1415\t<\n1416\tt\n1417\t)\n1418\t​\n1419\t1\n1420\t​\n1421\t[\n1422\tv\n1423\t∈\n1424\t𝒱\n1425\tmusic\n1426\t]\n1427\t,\n1428\t\\tilde{p}_{\\theta}(v\\mid c,x_{<t})\\;\\propto\\;p_{\\theta}(v\\mid c,x_{<t})\\;\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[v\\in\\mathcal{V}_{\\text{music}}\\right],\n1429\t(6)\n1430\tsampling until\n1431\tEOS\n1432\t, after which the deterministic inverse returns a guaranteed-playable score at any temperature. (iv)\n1433\tScale portability\n1434\t: the identical recipe runs from 0.8B to 27B, and one encoded dataset serves every scale. The recipe is deliberately minimal (single stage, no auxiliary losses, no RL), so measured quality is attributable to the representation.\n1435\tComponent 3: Ceiling-Anchored Evaluation Protocol\n1436\tThe protocol answers “is each design choice right?” with controls.\n1437\tRepresentation swap\n1438\t: seven tokenizations grouped by family,\n1439\tperformance-resolution\n1440\t(PMT and PerTok\n1441\t(Lenz and Mani\n1442\t2024\n1443\t)\n1444\t),\n1445\tbeat-grid\n1446\t(Beat-TSD, identical to PMT except timing; REMI; MIDI-Like, all via MidiTok with an identical base configuration\n1447\tincluding 32-level velocity\n1448\t, so the swap isolates timing quantization),\n1449\tgrouped\n1450\t(a Structured attribute-tuple control), and\n1451\ttext\n1452\t(ABC-as-text, whose web-pretraining prior\n1453\tfavors\n1454\tit), all trained under the same frozen splits, steps, batch, learning rate and decoding.\n1455\tCeiling anchoring\n1456\t: every texture metric\n1457\tm\n1458\tm\n1459\tis reported raw, as distance to the real reference, and as\n1460\tattainment\n1461\t, where for held-out real music\n1462\tY\n1463\ttest\n1464\tY_{\\text{test}}\n1465\tand encoder/decoder\n1466\tR\n1467\t,\n1468\tR\n1469\t−\n1470\t1\n1471\tR,R^{-1}\n1472\t,\n1473\tA\n1474\tR\n1475\t​\n1476\t(\n1477\tm\n1478\t)\n1479\t=\n1480\tm\n1481\t​\n1482\t(\n1483\tY\n1484\t^\n1485\t)\n1486\tceil\n1487\tR\n1488\t​\n1489\t(\n1490\tm\n1491\t)\n1492\t,\n1493\tceil\n1494\tR\n1495\t​\n1496\t(\n1497\tm\n1498\t)\n1499\t=\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "fa787f0e-de86-4690-a3fa-8cf13e967722", "uuid": "da7982fb-4c20-413b-b355-53d7a964f820", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T10:02:14.354Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/tmp/agogic_text.txt", "content": "[\n0\n,\n100\n)\n⊔\n𝒮\n,\n\\displaystyle\\sqcup\\ \\texttt{DUR}_{[1,201)}\\sqcup\\texttt{VEL}_{[0,32)}\\sqcup\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{[0,100)}\\sqcup\\mathcal{S},\n(1)\nso\n|\n𝒱\nmusic\n|\n=\n16\n+\n129\n+\n128\n+\n200\n+\n32\n+\n100\n+\n4\n=\n609\n|\\mathcal{V}_{\\text{music}}|=16{+}129{+}128{+}200{+}32{+}100{+}4=609\n. Formally, a piece\ny\n=\n{\n(\np\nj\n,\no\nj\n,\nd\nj\n,\nv\nj\n,\nc\nj\n)\n}\nj\n=\n1\nN\ny=\\{(p_{j},o_{j},d_{j},v_{j},c_{j})\\}_{j=1}^{N}\n(pitch, onset, duration, velocity, channel) is serialized in onset order as\nR\nPMT\n(\ny\n)\n=\n[\n\\displaystyle R_{\\text{PMT}}(y)=\\big[\nTSHIFT\nq\nt\n​\n(\nΔ\nj\n)\n,\n(\nTRACK\nc\nj\n​\nPROG\ng\nj\n)\n,\n\\displaystyle\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{q_{t}(\\Delta_{j})},(\\texttt{TRACK}_{c_{j}}\\,\\texttt{PROG}_{g_{j}}),\nPITCH\np\nj\n,\nDUR\nq\nd\n​\n(\nd\nj\n)\n,\nVEL\nq\nv\n​\n(\nv\nj\n)\n]\nj\n=\n1\nN\n,\n\\displaystyle\\texttt{PITCH}_{p_{j}},\\texttt{DUR}_{q_{d}(d_{j})},\\texttt{VEL}_{q_{v}(v_{j})}\\big]_{j=1}^{N},\n(2)\nwhich is\nschematic\n: the leading\nTSHIFT\ncarries the gap to the previous onset and is omitted when\nΔ\nj\n=\n0\n\\Delta_{j}{=}0\n, and\n(\nTRACK\n,\nPROG\n)\n(\\texttt{TRACK},\\texttt{PROG})\nare emitted only when the instrument changes (the exact run-length gating is in Appendix\nB\n). With base time unit\nτ\n=\n10\n\\tau{=}10\nms and backward inter-onset gap\nΔ\nj\n=\no\nj\n−\no\nj\n−\n1\n\\Delta_{j}\\!=\\!o_{j}\\!-\\!o_{j-1}\n(taking\no\n0\n=\n0\no_{0}{=}0\n), the three quantizers are deterministic and fixed,\nq\nt\n​\n(\nΔ\n)\n\\displaystyle q_{t}(\\Delta)\n=\nmin\n(\n⌊\nΔ\n/\nτ\n⌉\n,\n99\n)\n,\n\\displaystyle=\\min\\!\\big(\\lfloor\\Delta/\\tau\\rceil,\\,99\\big),\nq\nd\n​\n(\nd\n)\n\\displaystyle q_{d}(d)\n=\nclip\n(\n⌊\nd\n/\nτ\n⌉\n,\n1\n,\n200\n)\n,\n\\displaystyle=\\mathrm{clip}\\!\\big(\\lfloor d/\\tau\\rceil,\\,1,\\,200\\big),\nq\nv\n​\n(\nv\n)\n\\displaystyle q_{v}(v)\n=\n⌊\n32\n​\nv\n/\n128\n⌋\n,\n\\displaystyle=\\lfloor 32v/128\\rfloor,\n(3)\nso time-shift and duration share one 10 ms lattice and velocity is binned to 32 levels; simultaneous onsets give\nΔ\nj\n=\n0\n⇒\nTSHIFT\n0\n\\Delta_{j}{=}0\\Rightarrow\\texttt{TSHIFT}_{0}\n, so chords are runs of pitches at zero shift, longer gaps are tiled by repeated maximal shift tokens, and\nTRACK\n/\nPROG\nare emitted only on instrument change, giving\n≈\n4\n\\approx\\!4\ntokens/note (full procedure and a worked C-major-triad example in Appendix\nB\n). Two design choices define the representation.\nPerformance resolution\n: 10 ms time-shifts and 32-level velocities preserve the micro-timing and dynamics that beat grids quantize away, with clean model-free evidence in the round-trip\nonset error\n(\n2.3\n2.3\nms median on real music versus\n53\n53\nms for beat grids). The mechanism is precise: beat-grid tokenizers (REMI, TSD) place each onset on a tempo-relative grid of\nR\nR\nsteps per beat, encoding it as a bar index plus an in-bar position,\npos\n(\no\n)\n=\n⌊\n(\no\n−\nbar\n(\no\n)\n)\n/\nρ\n⌉\n,\nρ\n=\n60\nB\n⋅\nR\ns\n,\n\\mathrm{pos}(o)=\\big\\lfloor(o-\\mathrm{bar}(o))/\\rho\\big\\rceil,\\qquad\\rho=\\tfrac{60}{B\\cdot R}\\ \\text{s},\n(4)\nwhose step\nρ\n\\rho\nis\ntempo-dependent\n(\nB\nB\nis beats-per-minute) and bounded by the grid density\nR\nR\n(typically\nR\n∈\n{\n4\n,\n8\n}\nR\\!\\in\\!\\{4,8\\}\n, i.e.\nρ\n≈\n63\n\\rho\\!\\approx\\!63\nto\n125\n125\nms at\n120\n120\nBPM, coarser when slower). PMT instead encodes the raw inter-onset interval\nΔ\nj\n\\Delta_{j}\non the fixed\nτ\n=\n10\n\\tau{=}10\nms lattice of Eq. (\n3\n), independent of tempo and metre, so swing and rubato survive rather than snapping to a grid line. That single substitution, continuous performance time for quantized score time, is the one variable the controlled swap of Component 3 isolates. We also report a chord-time ceiling (\n39.1\n%\n39.1\\%\nvs. REMI/Beat-TSD\n35.5\n%\n35.5\\%\n, ABC\n32.5\n%\n32.5\\%\n) but read it with care: because the 10 ms lattice snaps near-simultaneous onsets to\nTSHIFT\n0\n, PMT’s ceiling sits within a couple of points of the raw reference and its sign is subset-dependent, which is why we treat onset error, not the chord-time ceiling, as the primary expressiveness signal (Appendix\nB\n).\nFlat single stream\n: unlike grouped encodings that need multi-head outputs, PMT’s stream is consumed by any single-softmax LLM, and it interleaves all instruments so the model attends across the full arrangement. Decoding is deterministic and total, so validity is\n0.99\n0.99\n–\n1.00\n1.00\n, and because every token names one parameter the representation is disentangled by construction.\nThe decoder is exact on the quantization lattice: encode\n→\n\\rightarrow\ndecode is the identity on quantized pitch, onset, duration, velocity and channel, so every deviation from a source piece is attributable to quantization, never to the serialization. Proposition\n1\nin Appendix\nB\nstates and proves this, with the error bounds (\n±\n\\pm\n5 ms onset,\n±\n\\pm\n5 ms duration,\n±\n\\pm\n2 velocity levels).\nComponent 2: LLM Integration Recipe\nThe recipe converts a pretrained text LLM into a text-to-music generator with minimal surgery. (i)\nVocabulary extension\n: the 609 music symbols are appended to the backbone tokenizer (Qwen3.5\n(Yang\net al.\n2025\n)\n, 248k text tokens) as mean-initialized embeddings, no architecture change, one softmax. (ii)\nCaption-masked SFT\n: each example concatenates caption tokens\nc\n=\n(\nc\n1\n,\n…\n,\nc\nm\n)\nc{=}(c_{1},\\dots,c_{m})\nand the music stream\nx\n=\nR\nPMT\n​\n(\ny\n)\n=\n(\nx\n1\n,\n…\n,\nx\nT\n)\nx{=}R_{\\text{PMT}}(y){=}(x_{1},\\dots,x_{T})\ninto one\n1024\n1024\n-token block\ns\ns\n. With a per-position mask\nℓ\ni\n=\n𝟙\n​\n[\ni\n>\nm\n]\n\\ell_{i}{=}\\mathbb{1}[i{>}m]\n, the backbone minimizes the\ncaption-masked\nautoregressive negative log-likelihood over caption–score pairs\n𝒟\n\\mathcal{D}\n,\nℒ\n​\n(\nθ\n)\n=\n−\n𝔼\n(\nc\n,\ny\n)\n∼\n𝒟\n​\n1\n|\n{\ni\n:\nℓ\ni\n=\n1\n}\n|\n​\n∑\ni\n=\n1\nm\n+\nT\nℓ\ni\n​\nlog\n⁡\np\nθ\n​\n(\ns\ni\n∣\ns\n<\ni\n)\n,\n\\mathcal{L}(\\theta)=-\\,\\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\\sim\\mathcal{D}}\\;\\frac{1}{|\\{i:\\ell_{i}{=}1\\}|}\\sum_{i=1}^{m+T}\\ell_{i}\\,\\log p_{\\theta}\\big(s_{i}\\mid s_{<i}\\big),\n(5)\nso gradients flow only from the\nT\nT\nmusic positions. Causal attention over the shared block means the music tokens still attend the full caption, so conditioning is preserved though the caption is not a prediction target. (iii)\nMusic-constrained decoding\n: at inference, logits are renormalized over the music range only,\np\n~\nθ\n​\n(\nv\n∣\nc\n,\nx\n<\nt\n)\n∝\np\nθ\n​\n(\nv\n∣\nc\n,\nx\n<\nt\n)\n​\n1\n​\n[\nv\n∈\n𝒱\nmusic\n]\n,\n\\tilde{p}_{\\theta}(v\\mid c,x_{<t})\\;\\propto\\;p_{\\theta}(v\\mid c,x_{<t})\\;\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[v\\in\\mathcal{V}_{\\text{music}}\\right],\n(6)\nsampling until\nEOS\n, after which the deterministic inverse returns a guaranteed-playable score at any temperature. (iv)\nScale portability\n: the identical recipe runs from 0.8B to 27B, and one encoded dataset serves every scale. The recipe is deliberately minimal (single stage, no auxiliary losses, no RL), so measured quality is attributable to the representation.\nComponent 3: Ceiling-Anchored Evaluation Protocol\nThe protocol answers “is each design choice right?” with controls.\nRepresentation swap\n: seven tokenizations grouped by family,\nperformance-resolution\n(PMT and PerTok\n(Lenz and Mani\n2024\n)\n),\nbeat-grid\n(Beat-TSD, identical to PMT except timing; REMI; MIDI-Like, all via MidiTok with an identical base configuration\nincluding 32-level velocity\n, so the swap isolates timing quantization),\ngrouped\n(a Structured attribute-tuple control), and\ntext\n(ABC-as-text, whose web-pretraining prior\nfavors\nit), all trained under the same frozen splits, steps, batch, learning rate and decoding.\nCeiling anchoring\n: every texture metric\nm\nm\nis reported raw, as distance to the real reference, and as\nattainment\n, where for held-out real music\nY\ntest\nY_{\\text{test}}\nand encoder/decoder\nR\n,\nR\n−\n1\nR,R^{-1}\n,\nA\nR\n​\n(\nm\n)\n=\nm\n​\n(\nY\n^\n)\nceil\nR\n​\n(\nm\n)\n,\nceil\nR\n​\n(\nm\n)\n=", "numLines": 600, "startLine": 900, "totalLines": 12535}}}
